          %h2#statement Statement
          %p
            Consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Top
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℝ
                  %msup
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C(-,\mathbb{R})
                  \\;\colon\;
                  Top \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}Alg^{op}
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebras"} associative algebras
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            given by forming
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+of+functions"} algebras of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            with values in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi Top
                    %mi cptHaus
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in Top_{cptHaus} \hookrightarrow Top
            are two
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} compact Hausdorff spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mi Alg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}Alg
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+homomorphism"}> algebra homomorphism
            ) of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(Y,\mathbb{R}) \overset{\simeq}{\to} C(X,\mathbb{R})
            arises as pre-composition with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"}> homeomorphism
            ) of the form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \;\colon\; X \overset{\simeq}{\to} Y
          %p
            In other words, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restriction"} restriction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Top
                    %mi cptHaus
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAA
                  %mi ℝ
                  %msup
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C(-,\mathbb{R})
                  \\;\colon\;
                  Top_{cptHaus} \overset{\phantom{AAAA}}{\hookrightarrow} \mathbb{R}Alg^{op}
          %p
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful functor
          %p
            It follows in particular that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} compact Hausdorff spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
            precisely if the algebras
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X,\mathbb{R})
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(Y,\mathbb{R})
            are isomorphic.
          %p
            In the literature, it is often this corollary alone which is referred to as the
            = succeed "," do
              %em Gelfand-Kolmogorov theorem
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(-,\mathbb{R})
